# Aven Interrupter taxes a spell an opponent casts from a graveyard by {2} (CR 601.2f). Bot1 flashes in Aven on its turn.
# On turn 2 Bot2 casts Faithless Looting from hand for {R} (the control: from hand, no tax). Flashback {2}{R} would be
# affordable with the four red mana of Bot2's Mox Rubies, but the cost is {4}{R}: the refusal. With a Mox Sapphire cast and tapped
# as the fifth mana the flashback is cast, and the five mana are all of it (the pool is empty with the spell on the stack); it is exiled by flashback.

[Bot1 Deck]
Mox Pearl x3
Aven Interrupter
Island x12

[Bot2 Deck]
Mountain
Mox Ruby x4
Mox Sapphire
Faithless Looting
Island
Island x12

